{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Phase 4a A/B: Delay Lama vs. Gervill",
  "intro": "Each comparison plays the instrument as midis2jam2 plays it (Gervill, its default soundbank) against Delay Lama candidates: first alone, then inside a small band (drums, bass, piano, lead) where the monk replaces that instrument. Every candidate is matched to the loudness of the instrument it replaces. The monk is dry (no echo); Gervill has its default reverb. The syllables are first guesses (phase 4c tunes them): judge the octave, and in c08 the dynamics. 'As written' means the monk sings the file's pitch (the helper adds the octave that the DSP drops); '-1 octave' is Delay Lama's native register. Guide: AB_LISTENING.md.",
